 1. Pull PC3's key log 

  ssh mhoang@172.19.140.43 'sudo cp ~/open5gs/logs/sslkeylog.log /tmp/sslkeylog-pc3.log && sudo chmod 644 /tmp/sslkeylog-pc3.log'
  scp mhoang@172.19.140.43:/tmp/sslkeylog-pc3.log /home/mhoang/Desktop/Mantis/sepp/sslkeylog-n32c.log

  2. Point Wireshark/tshark at it

  Wireshark: open your N32-c pcap → Edit → Preferences → Protocols → TLS → (Pre)-Master-Secret log filename → sslkeylog-n32c.log. Filter on http2.




